/**

@page page_installation_with_spack Installation with Spack

Spack installs everything from sources. This sets Spack apart from other
package managers. Spack downloads the source files, compiles them and places
the binaries inside of your system.
You don’t need to have *super-user’s* rights to install packages and
you can try different versions and flavours of them.

## Overview

We provide Spack scripts for various of Peano's extensions:

- [ExaHyPE 2](https://github.com/ExaHyPE-Engine/ExaHyPE/blob/main/utilities/spack/packages/exahype2/package.py)

## Prerequisites

Follow the official [Spack Installation Guide](https://spack.readthedocs.io/en/latest/getting_started.html).

## Getting Started

```shell
cd $HOME/Peano/utilities/spack
spack repo add .
```

To check the installation, query the available packages in Spack.

```shell
spack list exahype2
==> 1 packages.
exahype2
```

If you can see an output similar to the one above then we are ready to proceed.

## Usage

```shell
spack info exahype2
spack install exahype2 <OPTIONS>
```

### Installation Examples

```shell
spack install exahype2
```

Installs ExaHyPE 2 with the default settings.

### Uninstall

```shell
spack uninstall -y exahype2
```

## Remove the Repository

```shell
spack repo remove Peano
```

## Cleanup

```shell
spack gc -y
spack clean -a
```

*/
